Huh?  I don't understand the last sentence at all.

By "object tool", I mean a window that you could leave up at all times
that would always show what is in the ground at the current location.  You
could click on a button beside each object to pick the object up.  Or you
could click on a different button beside the object to mark it, and then
when you had marked some number of objects, you could pick them all up at
once by clicking on a button on top of the window.

   >8. The popup dialog box's insistence on appearing underneath the X cursor
