   I'm not sure what would have to be done to make the windows avoid the
   mouse pointer, and (in at least some cases) you want the new window to
   be in charge for its lifetime.  It's hard to say how to please everyone
   on this one.  To some degree, it might be up to the window manager to
   handle things.

Right now, it pops the window up with the mouse cursor in the exact middle.
Instead, it should pop it up so the mouse cursor is not over the exact
middle, but is instead over some blank space at the right or left edge of
the window.

